data/chords.json — the chord-voicing library behind the lead-sheet voicing modal.

Base: tombatossals/chords-db, lib/guitar.json — https://github.com/tombatossals/chords-db
      MIT License, Copyright (c) 2016 David Rubert
      (as shipped by quantumq1981/Parker-songbook-tool, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 ZembaCo)

Built by scripts/build_chords_json.mjs (deterministic):
  · every base shape is checked against the interval formula of the chord it is filed
    under; shapes that don't sound that chord are dropped (counts in main.validation);
  · qualities the base lacks are added (7#11, 13b9, maj7#11, m13, 9sus4, …);
  · each key × quality is topped up to 12 shapes from the engine's fretboard search
    ("generated": true).

